# .mcp.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It declares the collections-mcp server
# that `tools/collections-mcp/run-audit-job.sh` passes to `claude -p
# --strict-mcp-config`, so it defines the entire tool surface the autonomous
# audit job is allowed to touch collections/ through. Ignoring it meant a fresh
# clone couldn't run the job at all, and that the file governing an agent's
# write access wasn't versioned or reviewable.
#
# It contains no credentials today and must stay that way: if an MCP server
# added here ever needs a token, pass it via the environment rather than
# inlining it, or this file goes back to being unsafe to commit.

*.env

# collections-mcp per-run changelog (read by submit.mjs, never committed)
tools/collections-mcp/.changelog.json

# collections-mcp audit ledger — observational record of what the audit loop
# picked and what came of it. Local to whichever checkout runs the job; see
# lib/ledger.mjs for why it isn't committed (a file rewritten every run would
# conflict between concurrent audit PRs and jam the review cron).
tools/collections-mcp/audit-ledger.jsonl
